   "text": "This SMILES was read from the drawing. It describes a macrocyclic peptide with an 8-membered cis-alkene lactam ring embedded in the main ring.\n\n**Residues, in order around the ring**\n1. 4-CF3-phenylalanine, whose \u03b1-nitrogen is the lactam nitrogen of the 8-membered ring.\n2. N-methylglycine.\n3. A homophenylalanine bearing a 3-methoxy-4-CF3-phenyl group.\n4. A 4-methylproline.\n5. A 3,3-dimethylcyclobutane amino acid, with no stereocentre.\n6. N-methyl cyclopentylglycine.\n7. An N-methyl aspartate-derived residue whose C-terminus is an N-methyl-N-propyl amide.\n8. An N-methyl 2-amino-4-methoxybutanoic acid residue.\n9. Isoleucine.\n10. N-methylglycine.\n11. The N-methyl \u03b1-amino residue of the 8-membered ring, which carries the cis CH=CH.\n\n**Stereochemistry** was assigned from the wedges and hashes at each stereocentre, and the ring alkene is written as cis (`C/C=C\\C`).\n- Phe C\u03b1: S\n- Homophenylalanine C\u03b1: S\n- Proline C\u03b1: S\n- C4 of the methylproline: the wedged methyl fixes it\n- Cyclopentylglycine C\u03b1: S\n- Aspartate-derived C\u03b1: S\n- Methoxybutanoic residue C\u03b1: S\n- Isoleucine C\u03b1 and C\u03b2: both S\n- Azocine C\u03b1: S\n\nFor the isoleucine C\u03b1, the bold wedge could be read as pointing to the NH. I assumed that reading, and it gives the natural S configuration.\n\nSMILES: FC(F)(F)c1ccc(C[C@H]2C(=O)N(C)CC(=O)N[C@@H](CCc3ccc(C(F)(F)F)c(OC)c3)C(=O)N3C[C@@H](C)C[C@H]3C(=O)NC3(CC(C)(C)C3)C(=O)N(C)[C@@H](C3CCCC3)C(=O)N(C)[C@@H](CC(=O)N(C)[C@@H](CCOC)C(=O)N[C@@H]([C@@H](C)CC)C(=O)N(C)CC(=O)N(C)[C@H]3C/C=C\\CCN2C3=O)C(=O)N(C)CCC)cc1"
